<title>INDIA: Indian soybean prices rise, oils easy.</title>
<headline>Indian soybean prices rise, oils easy.</headline>
<dateline>INDORE, India 1997-01-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Fresh demand from processing plants propelled soybean prices higher on Friday in central Indian markets, traders said. Prices rose by 200-300 rupees per tonne but plant delivery rates were steady.</p>
<p>Soyoil prices eased on limited demand. Soyoil solvent and soyoil refined both lost 200 rupees per tonne.</p>
<p>Soymeal and rapeseed extraction prices were steady in very limited trading. Soymeal yellow was quoted at $278-279 per tonne in export while rapeseed extraction fetched $127-128. Rapeseed extraction was 4,350 rupees FOR Bedibunder and 4,300-4,325 rupees FOR Bhavnagar.</p>
